Copying over my comment from https://github.com/dotnet/runtime/pull/60060#issuecomment-936014202, it would seem like the key/value collection types in the generic `SortedDictionary` [do not implement `IList` either](https://github.com/dotnet/runtime/blob/main/src/libraries/System.Collections/src/System/Collections/Generic/SortedDictionary.cs#L567).

I'm wondering if we should be looking at #56835 more holistically and evaluate this proposal for sorted dictionaries in general. This would include SortedDictionary and ImmutableSortedDictionary. This might require discussion in API review.

@iRon7 I presume that your ask is not limited to `OrderedDictionary` but you would probably want to see this in all sorted dictionary implementations? Note that it would could not expose such an API in regular hashtables.
